{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "התחמס", :translit "ha-tachmas", :gloss "the tachmas"} {:he "חומס ואוכל", :translit "chomes ve-ochel", :gloss "it seizes and eats"} {:he "הנץ", :translit "ha-nes", :gloss "the falcon"} {:he "בעל נוצה הרבה", :translit "ba'al notzah harbeh", :gloss "possessor of many feathers"} {:he "ומנצח שאר עופות", :translit "u-menatze'ach she'ar ofot", :gloss "and overpowers the rest of the birds"} {:he "ותופשם", :translit "ve-tofesam", :gloss "and catches them"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Name התחמס explained as cognate with חומס, 'one who seizes'; and with מנצח/נוצה/הנץ as a wordplay cluster."}], :frame {:text "The Talmud identifies the tachmas (listed at Leviticus 11:16) as a bird of prey: 'The tachmas — this is the nes (falcon)' (Chullin 63a). The same passage derives its name from a root meaning 'to seize,' explaining that 'it seizes (chomes) and eats' its prey, based on the cognate root ח-מ-ס (Chullin 63a).", :sources ["Chullin 63a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Name התחמס explained as cognate with חומס, 'one who seizes'; and with מנצח/נוצה/הנץ as a wordplay cluster.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:51.936035956Z", :model "glm-5.2"}